# Regenerable from resources/branding/makehuman-logo.png by
# tools/make_appicon.py; only the .icns and the 1024 PNG are consumed.
resources/branding/AppIcon.iconset/

# Compiled corrective blobs, written beside their manifest. A DERIVED,
# host-endian cache (docs/formats/corrective-manifest.md, directive 12.4):
# rebuilt whenever the manifest hash moves, so committing one would put a
# machine-specific artefact under review for no benefit.
*.mhcorr
*.mhcorr.tmp

hair_research/

# RESTORED. LICENSING.md section 5.5 records this line as a safeguard the owner
# put in place before any of the Mixamo work: "It is gitignored (.gitignore:
# mixamo-asset/), by the owner, before any of this work began -- so the asset
# cannot be committed or shipped." It was briefly deleted when the folder moved
# under references/, which removed the safeguard without replacing it: a
# re-download into the old path plus `git add -A` would have put a
# non-redistributable Adobe asset into history permanently.
mixamo-asset/
references/mixamo-asset/

# The eyebrow reference sheet is LICENSED STOCK ART, used here as a ruler --
# `tools/make_eyebrow_hairs.py` measured its thickness profile and encoded the
# numbers. The numbers are ours; the artwork is not, and must not ship.
#
# NAMED, not a blanket `references/`. Seven Mixamo animation clips under
# references/ are TRACKED at the owner's explicit direction (LICENSING.md
# section 5.5), so a blanket rule would not untrack them and would silently
# swallow the next file added there -- which is the trap this file already
# records for `mixamo_superset.mhskel`.
references/different-shapes-colors-eyebrows-vector-illustrations-set/

# Scratch renders. Leading slash: only the one at the repo root, not any
# directory called `tmp` at any depth.
/tmp/
sample-locks/
